{"id":"eb747a15-acfa-47f6-a978-5bb425894cf1","object":"chat.completion","created":1784801044,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import math\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    if 'segments' not in payload or 'budget' not in payload:\\n        raise ValueError('Missing required fields: segments or budget')\\n    segments = payload['segments']\\n    budget = payload['budget']\\n    if not isinstance(budget, int) or budget < 0:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget must be a non-negative integer')\\n    if not segments:\\n        raise ValueError('No segments provided')\\n    # Validate each segment\\n    for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n        for key in ('name', 'importance', 'minimum', 'capacity'):\\n            if key not in seg:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Segment {i} missing field {key}')\\n        if seg['minimum'] < 0 or seg['capacity'] < 0:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Segment {i} has negative minimum/capacity')\\n        if seg['minimum'] > seg['capacity']:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Segment {i} minimum exceeds capacity')\\n    names = [s['name'] for s in segments]\\n    if len(names) != len(set(names)):\\n        raise ValueError('Duplicate segment names')\\n    total_min = sum(s['minimum'] for s in segments)\\n    total_cap = sum(s['capacity'] for s in segments)\\n    if budget < total_min:\\n        raise ValueError(f'Budget {budget} less than total minimum {total_min}')\\n    if budget > total_cap:\\n        raise ValueError(f'Budget {budget} exceeds total capacity {total_cap}')\\n    # Initialize allocations to minimum\\n    allocs = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    remaining = budget - total_min\\n    # While tokens remain, allocate to best segment\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_value = -1.0\\n        for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n            if allocs[i] >= seg['capacity']:\\n                continue\\n            # value = importance / (next allocated position = current + 1)\\n            value = seg['importance'] / (allocs[i] + 1)\\n            if value > best_value:\\n                best_value = value\\n                best_idx = i\\n            elif value == best_value and best_idx == -1:\\n                # first encountered tie, still set (should not happen because we check >)\\n                # but for tie even on first, need to handle\\n                pass\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            raise ValueError('No segment available to allocate remaining budget')\\n        allocs[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    # Build result\\n    allocations = [{'name': segments[i]['name'], 'allocation': allocs[i]} for i in range(len(segments))]\\n    name_mapping = [s['name'] for s in segments]\\n    total_allocated = sum(allocs)\\n    return {\\n        'allocations': allocations,\\n        'name_mapping': name_mapping,\\n        'total_allocated': total_allocated\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that implements coarse_budget_controller as described. The case payload contains segments with name, importance, minimum, capacity. Also budget. We need to allocate exact token budget. Steps:\n\n1. Validate: each segment has required fields, budget is integer, etc. If any missing or invalid, raise ValueError.\n2. Compute total_minimum = sum(segment['minimum'] for all segments). If budget < total_minimum: infeasible -> ValueError.\n3. Compute total_capacity = sum(segment['capacity'] for all segments). If budget > total_capacity: infeasible -> ValueError.\n4. Initialize allocations: each segment gets its minimum. Remaining budget = budget - total_minimum.\n5. While remaining budget > 0:\n   - For each segment, compute the next token's \"value\" = importance / (current allocation + 1). Since we are adding one token, the next allocated position is current allocation + 1. Actually \"importance divided 